Fold the paper in half along x=0.5 (valley, right half onto left), then fold the two-layer rectangle in half along y=0.5 (valley, top down). The result is a 1/2 x 1/2 square (area 1/4) and all four corners of the paper coincide at one corner of it. In the crease pattern, the y=0.5 crease reverses its parity on the flipped right half. So the only vertex (0.5,0.5) has 3 V and 1 M at 90° angles, which satisfies Maekawa and Kawasaki.

